## React Native Frontend Rules

### Component Structure
- **Functional Components**: Always use functional components with hooks
- **Props Interface**: Define TypeScript interface for all props
- **Default Props**: Use default parameters instead of defaultProps
- **Memo**: Use `React.memo` for expensive components
- **Hooks**: Extract complex logic into custom hooks

```typescript
// Example Component
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { View, Text, StyleSheet } from 'react-native';

interface ArticleCardProps {
  title: string;
  author: string;
  onPress?: () => void;
}

export const ArticleCard: React.FC<ArticleCardProps> = ({ 
  title, 
  author, 
  onPress 
}) => {
  // Component logic
  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <Text style={styles.title}>{title}</Text>
      <Text style={styles.author}>{author}</Text>
    </View>
  );
};

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    padding: 16,
    backgroundColor: '#fff',
  },
  title: {
    fontSize: 18,
    fontWeight: 'bold',
  },
  author: {
    fontSize: 14,
    color: '#666',
  },
});
```

### State Management
- **Local State**: Use `useState` for component-local state
- **Global State**: Use React Context for app-wide state
- **Complex State**: Consider Zustand or Redux Toolkit for complex state
- **Server State**: Use React Query or SWR for Firebase data
- **Avoid**: Prop drilling - use Context or state management library

### Firebase Integration
- **Service Layer**: Create dedicated services for Firebase operations
- **Hooks**: Create custom hooks for Firebase operations
- **Real-time Listeners**: Clean up listeners in useEffect cleanup
- **Error Handling**: Handle network errors and show user-friendly messages
- **Loading States**: Always show loading indicators during async operations

```typescript
// Example Firebase Hook
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { firestore } from '../services/firebase';

export const useArticles = () => {
  const [articles, setArticles] = useState([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [error, setError] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const unsubscribe = firestore()
      .collection('articles')
      .orderBy('createdAt', 'desc')
      .limit(20)
      .onSnapshot(
        (snapshot) => {
          const data = snapshot.docs.map(doc => ({
            id: doc.id,
            ...doc.data()
          }));
          setArticles(data);
          setLoading(false);
        },
        (err) => {
          setError(err.message);
          setLoading(false);
        }
      );

    return () => unsubscribe();
  }, []);

  return { articles, loading, error };
};
```

### Navigation
- Use React Navigation (v6+)
- Define navigation types for type safety
- Use stack, tab, and drawer navigators as needed
- Handle deep linking for push notifications

### Styling
- **StyleSheet**: Use React Native StyleSheet API
- **Consistency**: Define theme colors and spacing in constants
- **Responsive**: Use Dimensions API or responsive libraries
- **Platform-Specific**: Use `Platform.select()` when needed
- **Dark Mode**: Support dark mode using theme context

### Performance
- **FlatList**: Use FlatList for lists, not ScrollView with map
- **Memoization**: Memoize expensive computations with useMemo
- **Callbacks**: Memoize callbacks with useCallback
- **Images**: Optimize images, use proper resizeMode
- **Avoid**: Inline functions and styles in render

### Error Handling
- Use Error Boundaries for component errors
- Handle async errors with try-catch
- Show user-friendly error messages
- Log errors to Firebase Crashlytics
- Provide fallback UI for errors

