## Security Best Practices

### Frontend
- Never store sensitive data in AsyncStorage unencrypted
- Validate all user inputs before sending to backend
- Use Firebase Auth for authentication
- Handle auth token refresh automatically
- Don't log sensitive information

### Backend
- Validate all inputs in Cloud Functions
- Use Firebase Admin SDK with proper permissions
- Implement rate limiting for public endpoints
- Never expose API keys or secrets
- Use environment variables for configuration

### Firestore Rules
- Always validate data schema in rules
- Check user permissions before allowing operations
- Prevent data leakage through security rules
- Test security rules thoroughly
- Review rules regularly

---

## Environment Configuration

### Development
- Use `.env.development` for dev Firebase config
- Enable debug logging
- Use development Firebase project

### Production
- Use `.env.production` for prod Firebase config
- Disable debug logging
- Enable Crashlytics and Analytics
- Use production Firebase project

