## Common Patterns

### Loading States
```typescript
if (loading) return <LoadingSpinner />;
if (error) return <ErrorMessage message={error} />;
return <DataComponent data={data} />;
```

### Error Handling
```typescript
try {
  await firebaseOperation();
  showSuccessMessage();
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Operation failed:', error);
  showErrorMessage(error.message);
}
```

### Form Handling
- Use react-hook-form for complex forms
- Validate with Yup or Zod schemas
- Show inline validation errors
- Disable submit during submission

---

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

❌ **Don't**: Store large objects in state unnecessarily
❌ **Don't**: Make Firebase calls directly in components
❌ **Don't**: Use index as key in lists
❌ **Don't**: Forget to clean up listeners and subscriptions
❌ **Don't**: Use `any` type in TypeScript
❌ **Don't**: Hard-code strings (use i18n for user-facing text)
❌ **Don't**: Ignore TypeScript errors
❌ **Don't**: Skip error handling in async operations
❌ **Don't**: Store sensitive data in client-side code
❌ **Don't**: Use synchronous storage operations

